  "uncertain": [
    "SPI 2x3 header: pin names come from a separate detail drawing rotated 90 degrees relative to the board; the physical mapping (bottom row GND, GP11, 5V; top row RST, GP10, GP12, left to right) was inferred from that drawing plus rotated silkscreen text.",
    "Servo port: no rule settles the within-group order of the S/+/- columns for a 3xN header; S, +, - order used."
  ],
  "notes": "MAKER UNO RP2040 pinout (Cytron x ARUS): board render with callout tables. Labels are the GP (GPIO) names; silkscreen/Arduino names (A0, D7, S, SDA) first in functions, then callout columns outward. Recorded as printed even where callouts disagree between connectors (digital D20 shows RX1 while analog-side GP20 shows TX1; Grove 5 GP28 shows PWM6B while analog-side GP28 shows PWM6A). Servo '+' carries the note '*The value of + or VSERVO is depends on the power source supplied'. Skipped: USB-C, LIPO/LI-ON connector (+/- only), buttons, buzzer, LEDs."
}
